**What the patches do:**
1. In **Triangulation**, we drop the `sourceCoverageX < 1` check so that any quad spanning more than half the world (no matter how large) is treated as a wrap.  
2. We also tighten the shift threshold to `>= worldWidth/2` so that any triangle whose vertices genuinely cross the dateline get shifted back into a single continuous span.  
3. In **ReprojTile**, we now clamp both X and Y in the source‐extent before computing the tile‐range, which guarantees that the WebGL layer will ask for the tiles actually sitting just across the antimeridian.

With these three edits in place, the reprojection mesh will correctly cross the antimeridian and the layer will fetch and render all “missing” source tiles.
